/-- All-row vector-norm concentration for a deterministic signed-mixing family.

For each output row `i`, the coordinates are signed linear forms in the same
exact Rademacher vector.  The result applies the row-wise vector-norm primitive
and unions over rows.  It is an exact-probability foundation for finite
Rademacher/FJLT-style preprocessing branches; it is not by itself a floating-
point implementation theorem. -/
theorem rademacherTraceProbability_eventProb_forall_rowNormSq_signedMixingRows_le_ge_one_sub_sum_sum_two_mul_exp_neg_sq_div
    {r m n : ℕ} (G : Fin r → Fin m → ℝ) (U : Fin m → Fin n → ℝ)
    (T σ : Fin r → Fin n → ℝ)
